course: dictionary
lesson: 7392
title: Many meanings of plus
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Plus is a small word with several jobs. Its meaning changes with the words around it, so context tells you which meaning to use. «Two plus two?» is a sum, so here plus means add.
explain: Plus can also mean and also. «It is cheap, plus it is fun.» Try swapping in and also: «It is cheap, and also it is fun.» It still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: After a number, plus means more than. «Ages 8 plus» means eight and older. A plus can also be a good thing, an advantage, or a top mark, like an A plus.
fact: Plus means add: 3 plus 4 is 7.
fact: The sign for plus is +.
fact: Plus can mean and also, as in «It is cheap, plus it is fun.»
fact: A plus is a good thing, an advantage.
fact: «Ages 8 plus» means eight and older, and «A plus» (A+) is a top mark.
exercise: In «3 plus 4 is 7», what does plus mean? | Divide | Compare | *Add | Take away
exercise: «It is cheap, plus it is fun.» What does plus mean here? | *And also | Divided by | Before | Take away
exercise: Ella gets an A plus on her spelling test. What does this mean? | A late test | *A top mark | A low mark | A wrong answer
test: «Ages 8 plus» on a game box means which ages? | Only age 8 | Exactly 80 | Under 8 | *Eight and older
test: In «Quarter to three plus an hour and a half is 4:15», which sign shows plus? | Minus | = | × | *+
exam: Which sentence uses plus to mean and also? | «Two plus two is four.» | «Ages 12 plus is for older children.» | *«A squid has eight arms plus two longer tentacles.» | «See you later, à plus!»
